{"id":"fact-example-001","type":"code_quirk","fact":"Example: The UserService caches results for 5 minutes, so updates may not appear immediately in queries.","recommendation":"Use cache invalidation after writes, or query with { fresh: true } option.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"discovered during debugging","date":"2026-01-15"}],"tags":["caching","user-service"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/user.service.ts"],"affectedServices":["UserService"],"createdAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "fact-letsencrypt-paths-are-container-side", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "/etc/letsencrypt exists only inside the easy-proxy container; on the host it lives at $EASY_LETSENCRYPT_DIR, bind-mounted by easy proxy create. Running host-side commands against /etc/letsencrypt therefore fails with 'No such file or directory' and is easy to misread as missing certificates. The same split bites renewal configs: certbot writes ABSOLUTE paths into /etc/letsencrypt/renewal/<name>.conf, so a lineage created by a host-installed certbot (paths under the host dir) becomes unparseable once the same tree is mounted at /etc/letsencrypt inside the container.", "recommendation": "Run every certbot command through 'docker exec easy-proxy certbot ...', or use $EASY_LETSENCRYPT_DIR explicitly for host-side file work. Lineages inherited from a pre-container certbot cannot be repaired by editing paths piecemeal - reissue them from inside the container.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "production session production: first working IONOS DNS-01 integration + auto-renewal", "date": "2026-09-09"}], "tags": ["docker", "bind-mount", "letsencrypt", "certbot", "paths"], "affectedFiles": ["commands/proxy.sh"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-doctor-upstream-rule-false-pos-and-neg", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "easy proxy doctor's static vhost check keys off the presence of an 'upstream {}' block, which is the wrong predicate. Confirmed false NEGATIVE: a literal hostname in proxy_pass outside any upstream block (e.g. 'proxy_pass http://app_backend:8000;') is resolved at nginx startup and carries the identical whole-proxy outage risk, but is not reported. Confirmed false POSITIVE: an upstream block whose server is a literal IP (e.g. 'server 203.0.113.10:443;') has no name to resolve and no startup risk, yet is flagged - and 'fixing' it needlessly costs the block's keepalive.", "recommendation": "Rebase the rule on the real risk: warn when a proxy target is a DNS NAME resolved at startup (whether inside an upstream block or written literally in proxy_pass), and stay silent when the target is an IP literal or already a variable. See gotcha-static-upstream-blocks-nginx-startup for the underlying nginx behaviour.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "production session production: first working IONOS DNS-01 integration + auto-renewal", "date": "2026-09-09"}], "tags": ["doctor", "nginx", "static-analysis", "false-positive", "false-negative"], "affectedFiles": ["commands/proxy.sh"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-templates-lack-websocket-and-acme", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "The vhost templates rendered by 'easy proxy new http|https' (easyhome/templates/*.conf) only emit a plain 'set $upstream; proxy_pass $upstream;' location: no Upgrade/Connection headers (WebSockets break), no X-Forwarded-Proto, and no /.well-known/acme-challenge/ location (HTTP-01 impossible). easyhome/common.conf has the right maps and headers but is http-context only and is NOT included by easyhome/nginx.conf. In practice, real deployments end up hand-writing most vhosts.", "recommendation": "For apps with WebSockets or HTTP-01 certs, hand-write the vhost keeping the variable-upstream + resolver 127.0.0.11 pattern. Candidate repo improvement: template flags for websocket and acme, or include common.conf from nginx.conf.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "production operations", "date": "2026-09-10"}], "tags": ["nginx", "templates", "websocket", "http-01"], "affectedFiles": ["easyhome/templates/http.conf", "easyhome/templates/https.conf", "easyhome/common.conf", "easyhome/nginx.conf"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-09-10T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-10T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
